RUE.BAC++
========================================
Version: 0.2
Language: English
Purpose: Explain EXRUE and its relationship
to EXTYPOS, EXCOST, and
EXCOMMUNICATIONFAILURE.

----------------------------------------
CORE DEFINITION
----------------------------------------

SAV @EXRUE

EXRUE :

The operator state that occurs when the
cost of communicating an idea in English
exceeds the value of the communication.

Common Symptoms:

- Commit message fatigue
- Documentation fatigue
- Translation overhead
- English bottlenecks
- Desire to PUSH immediately

----------------------------------------
REFERENCE NODE
----------------------------------------

EXRUE=https://github.com/ess4654/The-RUE-Software-Challenge-

The repository acts as an external
reference source for the EXRUE node.

----------------------------------------
THE COMMIT MESSAGE PROBLEM
----------------------------------------

Normal Workflow

CODE
WRITE COMMIT MESSAGE
PUSH

Operator Workflow

CODE COMPLETE
IDEA COMPLETE
ENGLISH REQUIRED
EXRUE
PUSH

The code is finished.
The explanation is not.
EXRUE occurs during the delay.

----------------------------------------
EXRUE DEPENDENCY CHAIN
----------------------------------------

EXCOST<<>>EXFRUSTRATION<<>>EXCOMMUNICATIONFAILURE

Explanation:
As communication cost increases,
frustration increases.
As frustration increases,
communication quality decreases.
Communication failure becomes more likely.

----------------------------------------
TYPO CHAIN
----------------------------------------

EXCOST<<>>EXFRUSTRATION<<>>EXTYPOS<<>>EXCOMMUNICATIONFAILURE

Meaning:
Communication cost creates frustration.
Frustration creates typos.
Typos break dependency chains.
Broken dependency chains create
communication failure.

----------------------------------------
EXTYPOS
----------------------------------------

SAV @EXTYPOS

EXTYPOS does NOT primarily represent
spelling mistakes.

EXTYPOS represents:

- Dependency corruption
- Broken references
- Broken identifiers
- Invalid bindings
- Information degradation
- Context loss

----------------------------------------
DEPENDENCY EXAMPLES
----------------------------------------

EXRUE
does NOT equal
EXRUEE

Dependency chain broken.

EXARTBELL
does NOT equal
EXARTBEL

Dependency chain broken.

----------------------------------------

EXCOMMUNICATIONFAILURE
does NOT equal
EXCOMMINCATIONFAILURE
Dependency chain broken.

----------------------------------------
DEL TYPOS
----------------------------------------

Rule:
DEL TYPOS is a firewall.

Purpose:
- Preserve dependency chains
- Preserve references
- Preserve bindings
- Preserve signal integrity
- Reduce communication failure

DEL TYPOS is NOT a grammar operation.
DEL TYPOS is a dependency protection
operation.

----------------------------------------
GRAPH MODEL
----------------------------------------

EXRUE
<<>>
EXTYPOS
<<>>
EXCOMMUNICATIONFAILURE

Meaning:
The RUE Software Challenge demonstrates
that English itself can become a
development bottleneck.
As English overhead increases,
the probability of dependency corruption
increases.

